window.COURSE = {"title":"B1 revised scripts — six lessons (English)","version":"3.6.0-b1-reviewed-2026-10-07","documents":{"DOC-REQ":{"title":"NDT request (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Request / job reference (fictional: TS-V2)","Planned examination (day only, no calendar date)","Site / contact role (client's maintenance manager — Bram)","Component / drawing and weld IDs (vessel V-2; welds W-07, W-08; drawing V2-GA rev C)","Material (carbon steel)","Thickness / dimensions (12 mm / 1 200 mm — fictional sample values)","Examination extent (100 % of both welds)","NDT method (RT)","Examination technique standard (ISO 17636-2:2022, digital detectors)","Acceptance criteria (ISO 10675-1:2021; level per fictional project specification PS-V2 §6.5)","Attachments","Responsibility / confirmation (role only, no signature)"],"rules":"No default-standard fallback; method standard, acceptance criteria and legal justification are separate fields."},"DOC-TECH-JUST":{"title":"Justification of the technique (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Job / type of assignment (vessel V-2 shell welds, repair)","3a — Standard issued by a recognised standardisation organisation requiring radiography for this type of assignment: 'none identified'","3b — Contractual / project requirement: fictional PS-V2 rev C §6.3 'All circumferential butt welds in pressure-retaining shell plates shall be examined by radiographic testing over 100 % of their length.' (fictional teaching document — not a standard)","3c — Risk analysis of undetected fabrication defects: attached; RT selected for these welds (summary only, no values)","Prepared by (role: client's welding/NDT engineer — competent in NDT techniques)","Attachments"],"rules":"The selected legal route is 3c (KB IR art 3 §2); 3b alone never suffices; nothing is quoted from a real standard."},"DOC-LOC-JUST":{"title":"Justification of the irradiation location (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Workpiece / context (installed vessel on saddles; not movable)","Bunker — assessed: dismantling and transport for two repair welds assessed and rejected (reasons recorded) → not reasonably feasible","Irradiation infrastructure — none present; arranging fixed shielding around the vessel for these welds assessed (access on three sides only, crane traffic, duration) → not reasonably feasible","Conclusion for this type of assignment: another place (the hall), after risk analyses by client and company","Client's risk-analysis information for the company (hall occupancy, walkways, store behind the hall, crane use)","Associated evidence / attachments"],"rules":"Immobility, absence of infrastructure or ownership alone are never the stated reason; no transitional flowchart branch."},"DOC-LICENCE":{"title":"Establishment and operating licence — teaching excerpt","pages":2,"fields":["Authorised establishment / practice (industrial radiography in the company bunker and on clients' sites)","Installations covered","Equipment scope / inventory (placeholders, no numeric inventory)","Sources (placeholders)","Conditions","Evidence fields (acceptance, security acceptance where applicable)"],"rules":"Placeholders instead of real reference numbers; not blanket evidence that a job, site or person is ready."},"DOC-CERT-BUNKER":{"title":"Bunker conformity certificate — teaching excerpt","pages":1,"fields":["Description of the bunker and its location on the site","Permitted isotopes / maximum activity; maximum X-ray voltage and current (placeholders)","Permitted working configurations","Safety-logic reference (document with electrical diagram — referenced, not shown)","Validity (maximum 10 years)","Drawn up by: recognised expert in physical control (role only)"],"rules":"No stamp, signature, number or shielding dimension; this example has a roof; no universal roof rule."},"DOC-EXT-WORKER-FILE":{"title":"Pre-assignment information — external worker (teaching sample)","pages":2,"fields":["Page 1 — Sending employer: name / establishment unit / enterprise number (placeholders)","Page 1 — Worker: first name Clara; other identity fields as placeholders","Page 2 — Doses, last five calendar years, per year: 'provided' ×5","Page 2 — Doses, last twelve rolling months with monitoring period: 'NOT PROVIDED'","Page 2 — Non-uniform exposure / internal contamination: none declared","Page 2 — Assignment abroad: not applicable","Instruction / assignment scope (added by the operator): bunker and bunker X-ray set"],"rules":"'provided' / 'not provided' / placeholders only; a missing section is an evidence gap, not zero dose."},"DOC-AGREEMENT":{"title":"Signed agreement — external undertaking and operator (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Parties (roles only)","Clause A — Individual dosimetric monitoring and transfer of results to the exposure register: external undertaking","Clause B — Personal protective equipment: external undertaking","Clause C — Specific training on the controlled area and task: operator (not allocated)","Signature area: illustrative placeholders, no names"],"rules":"Allocates only what it names."},"DOC-CHECK-SHEET":{"title":"Pre-use check sheet — current version (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Instrument / device","Function check result","Date","Checked by (role)","Ambiguous sentence: 'Check the meter's response before/after positioning the device' (the sentence Daniel proposes to clarify)"],"rules":"The proposed revision sits beside it marked PROPOSED — not approved."},"DOC-CERT-AGENT":{"title":"Agent-course certificate (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Holder: Daniel","Theoretical training — knowledge test passed","Training body (placeholder)","Date (placeholder)"],"rules":"Proves the passed knowledge test only."},"DOC-PLANNING":{"title":"Worksite planning sheet (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Worksite / day","Team","Designated radiation protection agent (line)","Equipment","Client contact person"],"rules":"Designation is a recorded company decision."},"DOC-CONTROL-TEST-PROGRAMME":{"title":"Control and test programme — bunker safety devices (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Device: door interlock","Columns: Result · Date · Tested by","Previous month: satisfactory · date · name (placeholders)","This month: — · — · — (empty)"],"rules":"Result, date and operator name as KB IR art 15 §4 requires."},"DOC-HOLD-CARD":{"title":"Hold card (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["BUNKER USE ON HOLD","Reason: this month's interlock test result not established","Placed by (role) / informed (roles)"],"rules":"The visible held-work state; not tiny status text."},"DOC-CHANGE-REGISTER":{"title":"Change register of the physical control service (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Change description (additional X-ray set, type not in licence inventory)","Approvals given / still needed (expert countersignature; Agency decision)","Implementation status (proposal)"],"rules":"Per TR 6 Dec 2021 art 10; not every change shares one signature route."},"DOC-EVENT-RECORD":{"title":"Event account / handover record (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Observation (time, place, equipment, what happened)","Work / protective status","Contacted — and whether contact succeeded","Unknowns (cause; dose)"],"rules":"Unknowns are never converted into a cause, a dose or a permission."},"DOC-NOTIFICATION":{"title":"Written notification to the Agency — teaching sample (initial)","pages":1,"fields":["What / where / when; when discovered","Equipment and sources involved","Actual consequences incl. doses where known — 'dose under assessment'","Suspected causes (labelled suspected)","Urgent measures taken","Who manages the event","Physician follow-up / proposed INES level where applicable","Notifier (role)"],"rules":"Facts known at that moment; no zero for an unknown."},"DOC-CRITERION-EXTRACT":{"title":"Criterion extract — significant events (teaching card)","pages":1,"fields":["Criterion 1.5 — loss or failure of equipment fulfilling a safety function: direct contact by the next working day; INES evaluation yes","Criterion 1.4 — non-compliance with / unsuitable safety logic leading or possibly leading to unforeseen behaviour: direct contact immediately; INES evaluation yes","Written notification within 48 h for every event meeting a criterion","Source and date of the extract"],"rules":"Learning card; the procedure holds the complete current table."},"DOC-ASSIGNMENT-SLIP":{"title":"Changed assignment slip (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Worker: Clara","Requested: assist with gamma exposures, hall two, this afternoon","Requested by (role)"],"rules":"Shown beside the instruction record."},"DOC-INSTRUCTION-RECORD":{"title":"Specific instruction record — Clara (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Area: company bunker","Equipment: bunker X-ray set","Task: X-ray radiography of castings","Given by (role) / date (placeholder)"],"rules":"Scope is the evidence; a different area/equipment/task is outside it."},"DOC-PLANNER":{"title":"Job planner — week view (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Tuesday: client request received; written justifications received","Wednesday: company risk analysis completed; planning","Thursday (current day): worksite — vessel V-2, welds W-07/W-08"],"rules":"Current day clearly marked; plays automatically, not an exercise."},"DOC-SITE-PLAN":{"title":"Site drawing — client's hall (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Vessel V-2 position","Protection perimeter line (conceptual; no distances)","Walkway route (agreed) and changed route","Store behind the hall","Gate","Supervision positions"],"rules":"Conceptual planning drawing; no exclusion distances or dose values."},"DOC-FINAL-REPORT":{"title":"Final report — teaching sample (structure only)","pages":1,"fields":["Established causes","Doses","Detailed description","Preventive measures / lessons learned / action plan","Approvals where applicable (recognised expert; class 7 safety adviser)"],"rules":"Structure only; no content invented for the case."},"DOC-REG-EXTRACT":{"title":"Regulation extract page (teaching reader)","pages":1,"fields":["Article reference and short verbatim extract (Dutch) with English gloss"],"rules":"Used in the B1.1 exploration and reference readers."},"DOC-PROCEDURE-RECORD":{"title":"Approved procedure page with its approval line, and a record line (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Procedure title and version","Approved by: recognised expert (role)","Record line: what was checked · result · date · by whom"],"rules":"Procedure = method; record = evidence of a check on a day."}},"lessons":[{"id":"B1.1","title":"Getting started: radiation protection in Belgian industry","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome to the course","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Welcome to your radiation protection training. I'm Emilia, and I'll be your guide. Your own health, and the safety of the people around you, are at the heart of this course. By the end of it you will recognise where radiation risks arise in industrial work, know which responsibilities and checks apply before a job starts, and know when to stop and ask for help. We build that step by step, with examples from Belgian industry, and three principles will return in every example: justification, optimisation and dose limitation.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Approved Emilia beside the original cream, teal and gold illustration: trefoil connected to a balance, exposure-reduction shield and bounded dial. All visible from the start; no workplace photo.","beats":[{"at":"Welcome to your radiation protection training.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"I'm Emilia, and I'll be your guide.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"By the end of it you will recognise where radiation risks ar","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We build that step by step, with examples from Belgian indus","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"equipment":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"I work for an industrial radiography company, and that is the company we'll follow in this course. There, I lead the physical control service: the organised radiation-protection function of the company, the people, the checks and the procedures that keep exposure under control. You will meet my colleagues as they work: Daniel preparing an inspection, Clara arriving with her file, and Bram arranging a job at his site. Through their decisions we connect the Belgian rules with the information and the equipment in front of us.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Emilia introduces herself beside the principles illustration, with her name and role. No other participant is shown until named.","beats":[{"at":"I work for an industrial radiography company, and that is th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"There, I lead the physical control service: the organised ra","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"You will meet my colleagues as they work: Daniel preparing a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Through their decisions we connect the Belgian rules with th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"documents":["DOC-REQ"],"characters":["Emilia","Daniel","Clara","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We start with the framework and the people: who is responsible for what, and why protection has to be settled before work begins. Later lessons build the physics and apply it to more detailed situations. Take the course at your own pace: pause, replay an explanation, and keep your own notes. The practice questions along the way help you understand the decisions; they are not scored, and the final assessment is separate.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"A clean three-stop course route appears beside Emilia; stop 1 active.","beats":[{"at":"We start with the framework and the people: who is responsib","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Later lessons build the physics and apply it to more detaile","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Take the course at your own pace: pause, replay an explanati","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The practice questions along the way help you understand the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Before we begin, let me be clear about what this course is and what it is not. It gives you the theory: the knowledge you need if you work with radioactive sources or X-ray generators in Belgian class II industry. What it cannot give you is the rest: hands-on experience, instruction on the actual installation you'll use, and the responsibilities your employer assigns to you. Those come from your workplace. So when you finish these lessons, you'll understand the decisions; being appointed to a function, or allowed to use a particular piece of equipment, is a separate step that your company takes.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Emilia to camera; route fades to the two labels.","beats":[{"at":"Before we begin, let me be clear about what this course is a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It gives you the theory: the knowledge you need if you work ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Those come from your workplace.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"So when you finish these lessons, you'll understand the deci","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S01-P1","B1.1-S01-P2","B1.1-S01-P3","B1.1-S01-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"Where the course will take you","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Here is the road ahead, so you know where each lesson fits. The foundations come in three stages. The first stage is the one we're in now: the Belgian framework and the people who make it work. We start here, and not with the physics, for a simple reason: every protective measure you'll ever meet is a decision taken by someone with a responsibility, and you need to know who those people are before the rules make sense.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"One continuous three-part course route, with Framework and people active and the Belgian-framework illustration and summary visible.","beats":[{"at":"Here is the road ahead, so you know where each lesson fits.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The foundations come in three stages.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The first stage is the one we're in now: the Belgian framewo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We start here, and not with the physics, for a simple reason","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The second stage is radiation itself: where it comes from, how it behaves, and what the different quantities actually measure. That is where words you already hear at work, dose, dose rate, activity, get their precise meaning. With those ideas in place, shielding, exposure, biological effects and personal dosimetry stop being separate topics and become one story: how radiation reaches a person, what it does, and how we keep it low.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Continue in part 2 without restarting the route. Show Instruments and safety checks.","beats":[{"at":"The second stage is radiation itself: where it comes from, h","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"That is where words you already hear at work, dose, dose rat","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"With those ideas in place, shielding, exposure, biological e","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The third stage brings you to the equipment and the routines: the instruments you measure with, the safety checks you perform, and the way sources and contamination are handled day to day. From there, the class II modules take the foundations into more demanding situations: the authorised activity, equipment and safety systems, radioactive sources, more precise measurements, worksite arrangements and transport, and the response when something unusual happens. We won't ask you to solve all of that today; each module gives you something the next one can use.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Part 3 active from the first word; show the additional class II modules as applied knowledge.","beats":[{"at":"The third stage brings you to the equipment and the routines","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"From there, the class II modules take the foundations into m","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"We won't ask you to solve all of that today; each module giv","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Each part of the course is taught by a colleague whose own work fits the subject, so you hear the physics from someone who measures, and the routines from someone who performs them. For this first module I stay with you from start to finish, so that we can build on our conversation from one lesson to the next, and so that the people you meet today, Daniel, Clara and Bram, are still the same people when the situations become harder.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"A distinct four-part learning flow, not the course route again. Explanation, workplace example, decision and feedback stay visible.","beats":[{"at":"Each part of the course is taught by a colleague whose own w","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"For this first module I stay with you from start to finish, ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S02-P1","B1.1-S02-P2","B1.1-S02-P3","B1.1-S02-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"Who protects whom? The Belgian system","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let's begin with the people and organisations responsible for radiation protection in Belgium, starting from the outside. FANC is the Federal Agency for Nuclear Control: the public authority that regulates and supervises nuclear safety and radiation protection, with one purpose: to protect workers, the public and the environment from ionising radiation. For an industrial radiography company, FANC is the regulator. It grants the authorisations we need, it sets the rules, and through its inspections it checks that we comply. The protection itself is organised inside the company, by the people you'll meet next.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"FANC name and official logo","beats":[{"at":"Let's begin with the people and organisations responsible fo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"FANC is the Federal Agency for Nuclear Control: the public a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It grants the authorisations we need, it sets the rules, and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The protection itself is organised inside the company, by th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"equipment":["EQ-FANC-LOGO"],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P1","documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now step inside the company. Ours is an NDT company. NDT stands for non-destructive testing: we check whether a weld, a casting or a pipe is sound without cutting it open or damaging it. One way to do that is industrial radiography: we send X-rays or gamma rays through the part onto a detector, and the image shows cracks, voids or inclusions hidden inside the metal. That is why we work with X-ray generators and sealed radioactive sources, and why radiation protection is part of our daily work. A company that does this needs a licence for it. In the regulation the licence holder is called the operator, and the law places the responsibility for radiation protection squarely on the operator. To carry that responsibility, every operator must organise a physical control service, the service I introduced at the start. \"Physical\" here refers to the physics of radiation: the service controls exposure, from the equipment to the worksite. The health of the workers themselves is followed separately, through medical surveillance by a recognised physician.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Company frame highlighted; the word 'operator' appears on the frame.","beats":[{"at":"Now step inside the company.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"One way to do that is industrial radiography: we send X-rays","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"In the regulation the licence holder is called the operator,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The health of the workers themselves is followed separately,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"This is where I fit in. I am the head of that service. I coordinate and organise its work, and I have direct access to the head of the company: if a responsibility is unclear, or an issue needs to reach management, the organisation has to let me take it there. Beside my function stands another one, the recognised expert in physical control, and in a moment you'll see why I keep the two apart.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Emilia steps into the service area of the scene (supplied pose: standing, open hand).","beats":[{"at":"This is where I fit in.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"I am the head of that service.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"I coordinate and organise its work, and I have direct access","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Beside my function stands another one, the recognised expert","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The regulation reserves certain tasks for a recognised expert in physical control: a person who holds an individual recognition from FANC for a defined scope of work. Why an expert with a formal recognition? Because some judgements, whether a risk analysis is sound, whether a procedure gives enough protection, whether an installation may be put into service, must rest on expertise that the regulator has verified. A company may employ such an expert; ours does not. So, as the regulation requires, we have a contract with a recognised physical-control organisation: a specialist service provider, itself recognised by FANC, which carries out those expert tasks for us.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Company-to-organisation contract","beats":[{"at":"The regulation reserves certain tasks for a recognised exper","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Why an expert with a formal recognition?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A company may employ such an expert; ours does not.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"So, as the regulation requires, we have a contract with a re","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P4","characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P5","speaker":"Emilia","clip":"B1.1-S03-P5","text":"Two things are easy to blend, so let me name them separately. The organisation is the service provider: it holds a recognition and keeps meeting its conditions. The expert is a person employed by it, with her own individual recognition. In our arrangement, that expert performs the reserved tasks for our company: she examines and approves our radiation-protection risk analysis and our working procedures, for example. I coordinate our service; she brings the formally recognised expertise; and both of us work under FANC's supervision.","start_visual":"Individual expert inside the recognised organisation","beats":[{"at":"Two things are easy to blend, so let me name them separately","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The organisation is the service provider: it holds a recogni","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"In our arrangement, that expert performs the reserved tasks ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"I coordinate our service; she brings the formally recognised","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"screen_text":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P6","speaker":"Emilia","clip":"B1.1-S03-P6","text":"What does that look like in practice? The expert comes to our company for periodic evaluation visits, to see how radiation protection and safety actually work, and not only how they are written down. Depending on the visit, she examines equipment and safety devices, reviews dosimetry results and staff training, and checks our procedures and working arrangements. In industrial radiography that can include our own premises and observations at a customer's worksite; the exact scope follows from our activities and from the visit itself. Her job, in one sentence, is to connect what our records say with what happens where people work.","start_visual":"Why visit: evaluate radiation protection in practice","beats":[{"at":"What does that look like in practice?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The expert comes to our company for periodic evaluation visi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"In industrial radiography that can include our own premises ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Her job, in one sentence, is to connect what our records say","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"screen_text":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P7","speaker":"Emilia","clip":"B1.1-S03-P7","text":"After the visit, the company receives a written evaluation report. It records the findings and identifies the actions we have to take, each with a deadline. A report can grade how serious an issue is and show which actions are still open and which have been closed. The follow-up is mine to coordinate: we read the findings, carry out the required actions, and report back to the expert on what we have done. The organisation, in turn, has its own duties towards FANC. That is what gives the visit its weight: the expert's findings carry through into our records and, where needed, to the regulator.","start_visual":"Teaching report: findings, actions, deadlines and status","beats":[{"at":"After the visit, the company receives a written evaluation r","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"A report can grade how serious an issue is and show which ac","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The follow-up is mine to coordinate: we read the findings, c","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That is what gives the visit its weight: the expert's findin","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"screen_text":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P8","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now the people in the field: the industrial radiographers, sometimes called RT technicians, who actually carry out the radiography. In industrial radiography their training is built in. Every radiographer follows the training for radiation protection agents early in their employment, and only a radiographer who has followed it may operate gamma or X-ray equipment. So every radiographer is trained as an agent: one group of people, with two names for two sides of their work.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Daniel in the hall area of the scene with his handheld instrument.","beats":[{"at":"Now the people in the field: the industrial radiographers, s","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"In industrial radiography their training is built in.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Every radiographer follows the training for radiation protec","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"So every radiographer is trained as an agent: one group of p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"equipment":["EQ-HANDHELD-SURVEY","EQ-EPD-LEFT-CHEST","EQ-TLD-RIGHT-UPPER-CHEST"],"characters":["Daniel"],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P8"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P9","speaker":"Emilia","text":"On a worksite, the company goes one step further. From the trained radiographers present who belong to our own staff, it designates one as the radiation protection agent for that worksite. For those tasks, the agent works under our service. His job is the frequent, systematic checking of everyday protection: that the protection rules and work procedures are being followed; that the protective equipment, the instruments and the dosimeters are available, working and used correctly; and that any abnormal situation reaches me and the recognised expert. He does those checks according to instructions and procedures that the recognised expert has approved, which is how the expert's judgement reaches the worksite without the expert standing there.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Planning sheet DOC-PLANNING close-up: the 'designated agent' line with Daniel's name for Thursday.","beats":[{"at":"On a worksite, the company goes one step further.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"From the trained radiographers present who belong to our own","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"His job is the frequent, systematic checking of everyday pro","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"He does those checks according to instructions and procedure","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"documents":["DOC-PLANNING","DOC-CHECK-SHEET","DOC-PROCEDURE-RECORD"],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P9"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P10","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now connect the roles, and notice that they form a circle rather than a ladder. FANC regulates and supervises from outside. Our company organises radiation protection and remains responsible for it. I coordinate our service. The recognised organisation provides the recognised expert, who evaluates our protection and performs the examinations and approvals reserved for her. And on every worksite a designated agent checks and reports, under procedures the expert approved. The company keeps its responsibility alongside the expert's contract, and every radiographer keeps his own duties alongside the designated agent.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Regulator supervises","beats":[{"at":"Now connect the roles, and notice that they form a circle ra","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Our company organises radiation protection and remains respo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The recognised organisation provides the recognised expert, ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The company keeps its responsibility alongside the expert's ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P10","characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S03-P1","B1.1-S03-P2","B1.1-S03-P3","B1.1-S03-P4","B1.1-S03-P5","B1.1-S03-P6","B1.1-S03-P7","B1.1-S03-P8","B1.1-S03-P9","B1.1-S03-P10"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"The expert's report lands on my desk","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S04-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The recognised expert visited us last week, and this morning her evaluation report is on my desk. One of her actions reads: the working procedure for setting up a worksite has to be revised, because it no longer matches the way our teams actually work. She has set a date by which she wants to see it done. Nothing dramatic: exactly the kind of finding a good visit produces.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Expert visit: assess protection in practice","beats":[{"at":"The recognised expert visited us last week, and this morning","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"One of her actions reads: the working procedure for setting ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"She has set a date by which she wants to see it done.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Nothing dramatic: exactly the kind of finding a good visit p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S04-P1","characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S04-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Within an hour I have heard three opinions. Our managing director: \"We pay that organisation, let them write it.\" Luc, our most experienced radiographer: \"I know how it should read; I'll change it this afternoon and the teams can start using it.\" And Daniel, new to all of this, asking me which of the two is right. Think about who is responsible, who drafts, who approves, and when a procedure may be used.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Daniel considers the purpose of the visit","beats":[{"at":"Within an hour I have heard three opinions.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Our managing director: \"We pay that organisation, let them w","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Think about who is responsible, who drafts, who approves, an","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"}],"documents":[],"equipment":["EQ-FANC-LOGO"],"clip":"B1.1-S04-P2","characters":["Emilia"]}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S04-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Who does what to close this action?","prompt_spoken_once":"Who does what to close this action properly?","situation_visible_text":"The expert's report asks us to revise the worksite set-up procedure by a set date. The director wants the organisation to write it. Luc wants to change it himself this afternoon.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The recognised organisation writes the new procedure and issues it to the teams; that is the service we pay for.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"We do pay the organisation, and its expert will have a real part in this, just not the one the director has in mind. The procedure describes how our company works, and the responsibility for our protection stays with the company; so the drafting is ours, with the people who do the work. What the expert brings is the examination and the approval: she checks whether our revised procedure gives enough protection, and only after her approval do our agents work on the basis of it.","screen":"The company drafts the procedure; the expert examines and approves it; the company stays responsible."},"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Our company revises the procedure, the recognised expert examines and approves it, and only then do the teams work with the new version.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. I organise the revision with Luc and the teams, because they know how the work is actually done; that is the company carrying its responsibility. The draft goes to the expert, who examines and approves it, the task the regulation reserves for her. Until she has, the current approved version stays in use, and I report back to her before the deadline so that she can close the action. Three roles, one procedure, and everyone can say which part was theirs.","screen":"The company revises, the expert approves, the teams use the approved version. Until then the current version applies."},"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Luc revises the procedure today and the teams start using it; the expert reviews it at her next visit.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Luc's experience is exactly what the revision needs, and his draft is where I would start. What the draft cannot do yet is govern the work: our agents carry out their checks on the basis of procedures the recognised expert has approved, and a revised text becomes such a procedure only when she has examined and approved it. So the teams keep using the current version, the draft goes to the expert now, and her approval, not her next visit, is what puts it into use.","screen":"A draft is not yet a procedure. The expert approves it first; then the teams use it."},"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S04-P1","B1.1-S04-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S04-P2","interaction_id":"B1.1-S04-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"From Bram's email to a prepared request","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let me take you to Havenmeer Process Works. Bram is the maintenance manager here; his company runs this workshop, owns the equipment and knows the site. Havenmeer is our client: it asks our company to inspect some welds, and it will have to give us the information only a client can give. Our planning desk prepares the assignment with Bram before any of our radiographers goes to work, and that preparation is where radiation protection begins.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram at Havenmeer workshop","beats":[{"at":"Let me take you to Havenmeer Process Works.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram is the maintenance manager here; his company runs this ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Havenmeer is our client: it asks our company to inspect some","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Our planning desk prepares the assignment with Bram before a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"This is the steel vessel Bram wants inspected. The two highlighted rings are welds: they join sections of the vessel wall, and each runs all the way around. On his drawing they are numbered seven and eight. The vessel is one point two metres across and its steel wall is twelve millimetres thick. It is fixed to its supports and connected to pipework, so it stays where it is, which already tells you something about where the radiography will have to happen. Bram will have to explain that later, when he justifies the location.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Both welds highlighted on the vessel","beats":[{"at":"This is the steel vessel Bram wants inspected.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"On his drawing they are numbered seven and eight.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The vessel is one point two metres across and its steel wall","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Bram will have to explain that later, when he justifies the ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The job starts with an email. Bram writes: could you radiograph two welds on our vessel on Thursday? Please let me know whether this fits your planning. That is a familiar first enquiry, and it opens a conversation. Planning now knows what Bram wants; what it needs next is everything that lets us prepare the inspection properly.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Original short enquiry email","beats":[{"at":"The job starts with an email.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram writes: could you radiograph two welds on our vessel on","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"That is a familiar first enquiry, and it opens a conversatio","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Planning now knows what Bram wants; what it needs next is ev","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"So our planner replies with specific questions. Which welds, and how much of each weld must be examined? Please send a marked drawing, the material, the diameter and the wall thickness, and the examination requirements. We also need the exact location in the workshop, the proposed time, who else works nearby, and a contact person. To make that easy, planning sends Bram an inspection request form that puts those details in one place. Each line on it serves a purpose: the welds and the drawing tell us what to image, the material and thickness tell us how, and the location and the people nearby tell us whom we have to protect.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Planner asks for marked drawing and scope","beats":[{"at":"So our planner replies with specific questions.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Please send a marked drawing, the material, the diameter and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"We also need the exact location in the workshop, the propose","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Each line on it serves a purpose: the welds and the drawing ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P4"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram completes the request and attaches his drawing. Now every row matches something real: weld seven and weld eight, both in carbon steel, with the same diameter and wall thickness. He asks for the full circumference of each weld to be examined. He names the workshop and puts himself down as the contact person, reachable throughout the work, so that there is always someone on his side who can answer, decide and reach his colleagues. The law asks the client for correct written job information at least twenty-four hours before the work. That day is for us: it is the time in which we plan the exposure, mark out the area we keep clear, and agree who watches it.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram returns request and marked drawing","beats":[{"at":"Bram completes the request and attaches his drawing.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"He asks for the full circumference of each weld to be examin","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"He names the workshop and puts himself down as the contact p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That day is for us: it is the time in which we plan the expo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P5"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Planning also sends Bram a justification form. It asks for his reasons for requesting radiography, and for proposing this location, with the information that supports each reason. Bram gathers those answers with colleagues who have the technical knowledge, because the reasons have to hold up, in writing, for this type of job. We will read that justification in the next scenes; for now, notice who receives the form and why planning needs it back before we go further.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Planning sends justification form to client","beats":[{"at":"Planning also sends Bram a justification form.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It asks for his reasons for requesting radiography, and for ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Bram gathers those answers with colleagues who have the tech","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We will read that justification in the next scenes; for now,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P6"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P7","speaker":"Emilia","text":"There is a separate sheet as well: the task risk analysis, often called the TRA. Look at one issue in this workshop: a forklift route passes the vessel, and people use the nearby workbenches. Bram supplies that site information so that his company and ours can coordinate the precautions, and our company assesses the radiation risks on top of it. This sheet is about the hazards while the work is done. The justification form answers a different question, why radiography at all and what a missed defect would mean, and the two stay separate for that reason.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Separate TRA worksheet","beats":[{"at":"There is a separate sheet as well: the task risk analysis, o","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Look at one issue in this workshop: a forklift route passes ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"This sheet is about the hazards while the work is done.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The justification form answers a different question, why rad","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P7"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P8","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram returns the completed request, the marked drawing and the supporting documents. Planning brings the file together for the technical and safety review that follows. The first email has become a job we can assess, and the review is what turns it into a job we can do. Keep that sequence in mind: the client asks, planning clarifies, the client supplies the information, and our company reviews it. Next, we look at the reasoning behind using radiation.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram returns a coordinated file","beats":[{"at":"Bram returns the completed request, the marked drawing and t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Planning brings the file together for the technical and safe","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Keep that sequence in mind: the client asks, planning clarif","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Next, we look at the reasoning behind using radiation.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P8"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S05-P1","B1.1-S05-P2","B1.1-S05-P3","B1.1-S05-P4","B1.1-S05-P5","B1.1-S05-P6","B1.1-S05-P7","B1.1-S05-P8"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"Three principles working together","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P1","clip":"B1.1-S06-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram's request is now on our desk. Before we read his justification, let me show you how the three principles I named at the start work together, for ordinary, planned industrial work like this. Justification asks whether using radiation is warranted at all. Optimisation asks how we keep the exposure that remains as low as we reasonably can. Dose limitation sets the boundaries that may never be crossed. Each of the three has its own evidence, and a job is ready only when all three are answered.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Three linked responsibilities around the request","beats":[{"at":"Bram's request is now on our desk.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Justification asks whether using radiation is warranted at a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Optimisation asks how we keep the exposure that remains as l","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Each of the three has its own evidence, and a job is ready o","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P2","clip":"B1.1-S06-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Start with justification. Bram needs reliable information about these welds, because a defect that goes unnoticed could matter for the safety of the vessel. That is the benefit. Using radiation also brings disadvantages, among them a health risk, even at doses that cause no immediate effect, and the benefit has to outweigh them. A competent assessment therefore looks at what information the inspection must deliver and whether another suitable testing technique could deliver it. That reasoning has to be written down, for this type of job, by the people who can judge it; in the next scene we read Bram's.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Benefit: useful weld information","beats":[{"at":"Start with justification.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"That is the benefit.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Using radiation also brings disadvantages, among them a heal","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That reasoning has to be written down, for this type of job,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P3","clip":"B1.1-S06-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Suppose the use of radiography is justified. Then optimisation begins: keeping exposure as low as reasonably achievable, taking economic and social factors into account. For this vessel that means examining the practical arrangements before anyone starts. Can shielding be placed between the source and the people around? Can people work farther from the source, or spend less time near it? Can the forklift route and the workbenches be reorganised so that fewer people could be exposed at all? The inspection must still reach the quality the client needs, so the team chooses and verifies the measures under its procedures. And a reasonable improvement is worth making even when the dose would already stay well below a limit.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Shielding considered in the plan","beats":[{"at":"Suppose the use of radiography is justified.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"For this vessel that means examining the practical arrangeme","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Can the forklift route and the workbenches be reorganised so","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And a reasonable improvement is worth making even when the d","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P4","clip":"B1.1-S06-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Dose limitation answers a different question. For planned work, the applicable limits restrict the dose a person may receive over a specified period, for workers and for members of the public. A worker's record carries over from one assignment to the next: exposure from every job counts towards the same total. So a limit marks the boundary; below it, every exposure still counts and optimisation still applies. Planning and dose monitoring are how we keep that check alive during the work.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Dose limits apply over a defined period","beats":[{"at":"Dose limitation answers a different question.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"For planned work, the applicable limits restrict the dose a ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"So a limit marks the boundary; below it, every exposure stil","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Planning and dose monitoring are how we keep that check aliv","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P5","clip":"B1.1-S06-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now imagine someone answers our planner: \"The dose will be low, so we can go ahead.\" That sentence speaks to the third principle only, and even there it is an expectation, where the check asks for a documented comparison with the applicable limit. It says nothing yet about why radiography is needed for these welds, and nothing about which reasonable measures have been taken. The reverse is just as true: a sound justification still needs good protection. The three parts have to support one another.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Claim: low dose means proceed","beats":[{"at":"Now imagine someone answers our planner: \"The dose will be l","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It says nothing yet about why radiography is needed for thes","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The reverse is just as true: a sound justification still nee","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The three parts have to support one another.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P6","clip":"B1.1-S06-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bring that back to Bram's vessel. We need a sound reason for using radiation, practical arrangements that reduce exposure, and respect for the applicable dose limits, and each of the three stands on its own evidence, so the file is finished only when all three are. That is the framework for the lessons that follow. First we examine justification and who has to provide it. Then we look more closely at optimisation in preparing the job.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Reason for using radiation","beats":[{"at":"Bring that back to Bram's vessel.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"We need a sound reason for using radiation, practical arrang","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"First we examine justification and who has to provide it.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Then we look more closely at optimisation in preparing the j","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S06-P1","B1.1-S06-P2","B1.1-S06-P3","B1.1-S06-P4","B1.1-S06-P5","B1.1-S06-P6"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"Justification: from the request to the work location","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P1","clip":"B1.1-S07-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let's review Bram's request properly, instead of putting it in the diary. The Belgian Royal Decree of the seventeenth of February, twenty twenty-three, on industrial radiography asks three justification questions for every assignment. Why this examination technique? Why this irradiation location? And why this equipment? The first two belong to the client: Havenmeer gives us its written justification of the technique and of the location, for each type of assignment. The third belongs to us: our company justifies the equipment, and decides whether it can accept the assignment at all. You can open the legal references below as we go.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Three written decisions","beats":[{"at":"Let's review Bram's request properly, instead of putting it ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Why this examination technique?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The first two belong to the client: Havenmeer gives us its w","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"You can open the legal references below as we go.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P2","clip":"B1.1-S07-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"First, why radiography for these welds? Article three gives two routes. The first: a specific industrial standard, issued by a recognised standardisation organisation, requires radiography for this type of assignment; then the client identifies that requirement, standard and clause. The second: where no industrial standard provides for radiography, or the client asks for more than the standard does, the client justifies radiography with a risk analysis of what it would mean if a fabrication defect went undetected. Two documents are easy to mistake for that analysis, so know them: a purchase order that says \"please do X-ray\" tells us what the client wants; a standard that explains how to take a radiograph tells us how to do it well. The justification is the reasoning behind the choice, and that is what we read.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Two routes under article 3","beats":[{"at":"First, why radiography for these welds?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The first: a specific industrial standard, issued by a recog","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The second: where no industrial standard provides for radiog","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The justification is the reasoning behind the choice, and th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P3","clip":"B1.1-S07-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"In Bram's file, no industrial standard requiring radiography has been identified for these two welds. His project specification asks for radiography, so the second route applies: his reasoned risk analysis. Its subject is a weld that holds pressure: what a missed defect could lead to, and whether another examination technique could give the same assurance. Keep this apart from the task risk assessment about forklifts, access and other workshop hazards: both matter, and they answer different questions. We read the reasoning in the analysis; the label \"project requirement\" on the specification is where that reasoning starts, and the analysis is where it is made.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram: risk-analysis route","beats":[{"at":"In Bram's file, no industrial standard requiring radiography","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"His project specification asks for radiography, so the secon","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Keep this apart from the task risk assessment about forklift","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We read the reasoning in the analysis; the label \"project re","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P4","clip":"B1.1-S07-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Next, where should the work take place? Article four gives a firm rule for small movable workpieces: if the complete workpiece fits within one cubic metre and weighs less than five hundred kilograms, its radiography takes place in a bunker: both conditions together, and the piece has to be movable. Look at this separate small pipe assembly: eighty by sixty by forty centimetres, one hundred and twenty kilograms. It meets the conditions, so it goes to a bunker. Note that we judge the complete workpiece, because the whole piece is what travels, and the short length of weld being examined is only the part we image. Our company also checks that the bunker holds a valid conformity certificate.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Movable complete workpiece","beats":[{"at":"Next, where should the work take place?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Look at this separate small pipe assembly: eighty by sixty b","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It meets the conditions, so it goes to a bunker.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Our company also checks that the bunker holds a valid confor","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P5","clip":"B1.1-S07-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"For a larger or heavier workpiece, a bunker is still the preferred location. Where that is not reasonably feasible, the next option is an irradiation infrastructure at the client's site, after risk analyses by both the client and our company. An irradiation infrastructure is a real facility: fixed shielding built for radiation protection, with the required safety arrangements and supervised entrances; shielding and control, in other words, that stand between the radiation and everyone else. Only when neither a bunker nor such an infrastructure is reasonably feasible may another location be considered, again after both risk analyses. The client records the location justification in writing.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bunker first","beats":[{"at":"For a larger or heavier workpiece, a bunker is still the pre","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Where that is not reasonably feasible, the next option is an","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Only when neither a bunker nor such an infrastructure is rea","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The client records the location justification in writing.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P6","clip":"B1.1-S07-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now apply that order to Bram's vessel. It is one point two metres across and installed in the workshop; welds seven and eight are part of it, so the vessel as a whole is the workpiece. The file therefore examines dismantling and transporting the vessel to a bunker, and explains why that is not reasonably feasible here. It then examines whether fixed shielding could be provided at the vessel, and explains the outcome. Those two supported assessments are what carry the choice of the hall. Bram supplies the site information; our company reviews the proposed conditions and decides whether it can accept them.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Two welds remain part of the vessel","beats":[{"at":"Now apply that order to Bram's vessel.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The file therefore examines dismantling and transporting the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It then examines whether fixed shielding could be provided a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Bram supplies the site information; our company reviews the ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P7","clip":"B1.1-S07-P7","speaker":"Emilia","text":"If the hall is justified, the radiation still needs a protected work area. Before the radiography, the team marks out a continuous protection perimeter, using at least barrier tape and ionising-radiation warning signs, with a warning lamp in darkness or poor visibility. Look beyond the vessel: workshop doors, nearby benches and every route into the area are part of the picture. Bram is told where the perimeter will run. The client and our company agree in advance who will supervise it, with extra people wherever the radiographers cannot watch the whole line themselves. The tape marks the boundary; the protection comes from the distance it creates, which is why the one thing that matters is that nobody crosses it. And work outside a bunker is always done by at least two industrial radiographers.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Continuous barrier around work","beats":[{"at":"If the hall is justified, the radiation still needs a protec","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Look beyond the vessel: workshop doors, nearby benches and e","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The client and our company agree in advance who will supervi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And work outside a bunker is always done by at least two ind","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P8","clip":"B1.1-S07-P8","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Where that boundary runs follows from a measurement, under article nineteen. The dose rate outside the perimeter is limited according to who is there: ten microsieverts per hour where people work permanently and in adjoining buildings, forty where workstations are only occasionally occupied, because someone who spends the whole day at a bench must be protected more than someone who passes by. Repeated work at the same place must also respect the three-hundred-microsievert yearly constraint for each person who is not occupationally exposed. The team measures at the perimeter during the first exposure or a test exposure and enlarges the area if the reading asks for it. These values are ceilings; optimisation, which we look at next, works below them.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Permanent workplaces and adjoining buildings","beats":[{"at":"Where that boundary runs follows from a measurement, under a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The dose rate outside the perimeter is limited according to ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The team measures at the perimeter during the first exposure","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"These values are ceilings; optimisation, which we look at ne","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P9","clip":"B1.1-S07-P9","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Finally, our company justifies the equipment. Article five prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasible without creating additional risk. Where gamma radiography is used, the isotope's penetrating power has to suit the examination. As head of our physical control service, I make sure that a person competent in the different NDT techniques has justified the technique, the isotope and the activity for each assignment, so the equipment is chosen for the job, with reasons. And if our company cannot accept the client's justification of the technique or of the location, it refuses the assignment.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"X-ray preference with conditions","beats":[{"at":"Finally, our company justifies the equipment.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Article five prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasibl","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"As head of our physical control service, I make sure that a ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And if our company cannot accept the client's justification ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P10","clip":"B1.1-S07-P10","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram's request can now be read as a connected file: a reason for radiography, a supported location choice, our equipment assessment, and agreed protection arrangements; four pieces of evidence, each standing on its own. In the workshop, the required measures and the last-minute risk assessment still have to be in place, and if safe working turns out to be impossible, the radiographers stop and report it immediately. Before we move on to optimisation, let me place three workpieces for you. The small pipe assembly, movable, within the size and under the weight: the bunker. A heavy frame that could be moved but would not fit a bunker: a bunker where reasonably feasible, otherwise an irradiation infrastructure after both risk analyses. Bram's installed vessel: the hall, on the strength of the two assessments we just read. Notice that wall thickness played no part in placing them: it helps us choose the examination technique, and it is not part of the bunker rule.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Connected evidence","beats":[{"at":"Bram's request can now be read as a connected file: a reason","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Before we move on to optimisation, let me place three workpi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A heavy frame that could be moved but would not fit a bunker","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Notice that wall thickness played no part in placing them: i","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S07-Q01","type":"case_sequence","title_visible":"Who justifies what?","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram calls you about his request. Three of his questions, three answers to choose. Each answer is explained.","cases":[{"id":"case1","title":"The technique","situation_visible_text":"Bram: \"You're the radiography specialists. Can't you simply confirm that these welds need radiography, so I don't have to write anything?\"","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram asks: you are the radiography specialists, can't you simply confirm that these welds need radiography, so he doesn't have to write anything? What do you tell him?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: our head of service confirms the technique for every job, so his written justification is covered by ours.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Our head of service does check every job: she makes sure a competent person justified the technique, isotope and activity. That is our company's verification of a justification that already exists. The justification itself is the client's: for each type of assignment, Bram puts in writing why radiography is the right method, either because a standard from a recognised standardisation organisation requires it, or, as here, through his risk analysis of what an undetected defect would mean. We check his reasoning; we cannot write it for him.","screen":"Our head of service does check every job: she makes sure a competent person justified the technique, isotope and activity. That is our company's verification of a justification that already exists. The justification itself is the client's: for each type of assignment, Bram puts in writing why radiography is the right method, either because a standard from a recognised standardisation organisation requires it, or, as here, through his risk analysis of what an undetected defect would mean. We check his reasoning; we cannot write it for him."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1-a"},{"id":"b","text":"No: the technique justification is the client's, in writing: a standard that requires radiography, or his risk analysis of undetected defects.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The decree gives Bram two routes: a specific industrial standard from a recognised standardisation organisation that requires radiography for this type of assignment, or, where no such standard provides for it, a risk analysis of what it would mean if a fabrication defect went undetected in these pressure-holding welds. For his vessel no such standard has been identified, so it is the risk analysis, prepared with people who can judge it. Our part comes afterwards: we verify it, and we refuse the job if we cannot accept it.","screen":"Yes. The decree gives Bram two routes: a specific industrial standard from a recognised standardisation organisation that requires radiography for this type of assignment, or, where no such standard provides for it, a risk analysis of what it would mean if a fabrication defect went undetected in these pressure-holding welds. For his vessel no such standard has been identified, so it is the risk analysis, prepared with people who can judge it. Our part comes afterwards: we verify it, and we refuse the job if we cannot accept it."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1-b"},{"id":"c","text":"No, but his project specification already says \"all shell welds shall be radiographed\", and that sentence is the justification.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The specification is a real document and it matters: it tells us what Bram requires of his welds. What it does not contain is the reasoning the decree asks for. A requirement in his own project document is not a standard issued by a recognised standardisation organisation, so it does not open the first route; and it is not a risk analysis, so it does not complete the second. The specification is where Bram's reasoning starts; the risk analysis is where he makes it.","screen":"The specification is a real document and it matters: it tells us what Bram requires of his welds. What it does not contain is the reasoning the decree asks for. A requirement in his own project document is not a standard issued by a recognised standardisation organisation, so it does not open the first route; and it is not a risk analysis, so it does not complete the second. The specification is where Bram's reasoning starts; the risk analysis is where he makes it."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1"},{"id":"case2","title":"The location","situation_visible_text":"Bram: \"The vessel is welded in place and we have no bunker, so the hall is the only option. Is that enough for the location?\"","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram says: the vessel is welded in place and we have no bunker, so the hall is the only option. Is that enough for the location? What do you tell him?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: a fixed vessel cannot go to a bunker, so the firm bunker rule does not apply and the hall follows.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Right about the rule: the firm requirement is for small, movable workpieces, and this vessel is neither small nor movable. Outside that rule the decree sets an order, not a free choice: a bunker is still preferred, then an irradiation infrastructure at the site, and only when neither is reasonably feasible another place. Bram's justification has to walk that order with reasons, why dismantling and transport are unreasonable, why fixed shielding at the vessel is not feasible, before the hall is the answer.","screen":"Right about the rule: the firm requirement is for small, movable workpieces, and this vessel is neither small nor movable. Outside that rule the decree sets an order, not a free choice: a bunker is still preferred, then an irradiation infrastructure at the site, and only when neither is reasonably feasible another place. Bram's justification has to walk that order with reasons, why dismantling and transport are unreasonable, why fixed shielding at the vessel is not feasible, before the hall is the answer."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Yes, as long as our company adds its own risk analysis of the hall to his file.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Our risk analysis is required and we will make it. It answers how we work safely at a place, once that place is justified. Justifying the place is Bram's task, in writing, and the decree asks him for two assessments: whether taking the vessel to a bunker is reasonably feasible, and whether fixed shielding at the vessel is. Both risk analyses, his and ours, then support the hall. His sentence gives the facts; the assessments give the justification.","screen":"Our risk analysis is required and we will make it. It answers how we work safely at a place, once that place is justified. Justifying the place is Bram's task, in writing, and the decree asks him for two assessments: whether taking the vessel to a bunker is reasonably feasible, and whether fixed shielding at the vessel is. Both risk analyses, his and ours, then support the hall. His sentence gives the facts; the assessments give the justification."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Not yet: his written justification has to assess both the bunker and fixed shielding at the vessel, with reasons, before the hall is justified.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. \"Welded in place\" and \"no bunker on site\" are facts; the justification is the reasoning the decree asks for. Bram's file has to show why dismantling and transport to a bunker are not reasonably feasible, and why an irradiation infrastructure, fixed shielding at the vessel, is not either. With those two assessments in writing, and risk analyses from both companies, the hall is the justified location, and the perimeter and its supervision are planned there.","screen":"Exactly. \"Welded in place\" and \"no bunker on site\" are facts; the justification is the reasoning the decree asks for. Bram's file has to show why dismantling and transport to a bunker are not reasonably feasible, and why an irradiation infrastructure, fixed shielding at the vessel, is not either. With those two assessments in writing, and risk analyses from both companies, the hall is the justified location, and the perimeter and its supervision are planned there."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2"},{"id":"case3","title":"The equipment","situation_visible_text":"Bram: \"Will you be using X-rays or a gamma source for my welds? And is that my decision or yours?\"","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram asks: X-rays or a gamma source for his welds, and is that his decision or ours? What do you tell him?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Ours: our company justifies the equipment, preferring an X-ray generator where that is feasible without extra risk, and matching the isotope to the examination where gamma is used.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The third justification question belongs to our company. The decree prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasible without creating additional risk; where gamma radiography is used, the isotope's penetrating power has to suit the examination. Our head of service makes sure a person competent in the NDT techniques justified the technique, the isotope and the activity for this assignment. Bram hears what we chose and why; the choice and its reasons are ours.","screen":"Yes. The third justification question belongs to our company. The decree prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasible without creating additional risk; where gamma radiography is used, the isotope's penetrating power has to suit the examination. Our head of service makes sure a person competent in the NDT techniques justified the technique, the isotope and the activity for this assignment. Bram hears what we chose and why; the choice and its reasons are ours."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3-a"},{"id":"b","text":"His: the client justifies technique and location, and the equipment is part of the technique.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Half right: Bram does justify the technique, why radiography, and the location. The equipment is the third, separate question, and the decree gives it to the company doing the work, because it depends on our generators, our sources and our competence. So Bram justifies that radiography is needed and where; we justify what we bring, with a preference for X-rays where feasible without extra risk.","screen":"Half right: Bram does justify the technique, why radiography, and the location. The equipment is the third, separate question, and the decree gives it to the company doing the work, because it depends on our generators, our sources and our competence. So Bram justifies that radiography is needed and where; we justify what we bring, with a preference for X-rays where feasible without extra risk."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Neither: FANC decides which equipment may be used on a client's site.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"FANC is in the picture, as the regulator that licensed our equipment and can prohibit a location it finds insufficiently justified. The choice of equipment for a given assignment, though, is made by our company, under the decree's rule: X-ray generator where feasible without extra risk, and a suitable isotope where gamma is used, justified by a competent person and checked by our head of service. We decide; FANC supervises.","screen":"FANC is in the picture, as the regulator that licensed our equipment and can prohibit a location it finds insufficiently justified. The choice of equipment for a given assignment, though, is made by our company, under the decree's rule: X-ray generator where feasible without extra risk, and a suitable isotope where gamma is used, justified by a competent person and checked by our head of service. We decide; FANC supervises."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S07-P1","B1.1-S07-P2","B1.1-S07-P3","B1.1-S07-P4","B1.1-S07-P5","B1.1-S07-P6","B1.1-S07-P7","B1.1-S07-P8","B1.1-S07-P9","B1.1-S07-P10"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S07-P10","interaction_id":"B1.1-S07-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"Optimisation: protecting people in Bram's hall","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We are back in Bram's workshop at Havenmeer. For this example, the reasons for examining the installed vessel here have been accepted. Now we improve the way the job will be done. Optimisation means keeping exposure as low as reasonably achievable, taking economic and social factors into account: looking, below the limits, for every reasonable improvement. Daniel and Sofia are our radiography team. With Bram, they prepare the positions, the shielding and the access arrangements before any exposure.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"We are back in Bram's workshop at Havenmeer.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Now we improve the way the job will be done.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Optimisation means keeping exposure as low as reasonably ach","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"With Bram, they prepare the positions, the shielding and the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Start with the radiation itself, before the barrier tape. The team chooses a beam direction that points away from where people are, and restricts the beam so that only the weld and its surroundings are irradiated. Here, a lead shielding screen is placed between the examination area and the proposed control position. Its material, thickness and position have to suit the equipment and the assessed radiation field, including scattered radiation, because radiation that hits the vessel and the floor bounces off in other directions and reaches places the direct beam never pointed at. The screen takes a large share of the exposure out of the control position; the perimeter around the whole set-up takes care of everyone else.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Start with the radiation itself, before the barrier tape.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The team chooses a beam direction that points away from wher","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Its material, thickness and position have to suit the equipm","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The screen takes a large share of the exposure out of the co","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now look at Daniel's position. The controls are placed away from the vessel, outside the protection perimeter, with the shielding between him and the examination area. Increasing distance usually reduces exposure. For an unshielded point source in free space, twice the distance gives roughly a quarter of the dose rate; scattering and shielding in this hall change that simple relationship. The exact positions follow from the assessment and are confirmed by measurement on the day. Sofia watches the other approach from outside the perimeter. The two radiographers stay in visual or audible contact with each other throughout, and extra supervision is arranged wherever they cannot cover all the access routes themselves.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Now look at Daniel's position.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Increasing distance usually reduces exposure.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The exact positions follow from the assessment and are confi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The two radiographers stay in visual or audible contact with","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The pedestrian route is another part of the job. People normally use it to reach the workbenches. Bram arranges for those activities to stop and for the route to be closed during the exposures. The closure is agreed in advance, marked, and supervised, so that it holds even when someone is in a hurry. Daniel covers the control-side approach and Sofia the other entrance. The team starts only when both routes are controlled, and if someone crosses the boundary during an exposure, the exposure is stopped first and the conversation comes afterwards.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"The pedestrian route is another part of the job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram arranges for those activities to stop and for the route","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The closure is agreed in advance, marked, and supervised, so","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The team starts only when both routes are controlled, and if","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P4"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Good preparation also keeps exposure time down. Before any radiation is produced, the team checks the weld identification, the detector position, the equipment and the exposure plan, so that each image is taken once and taken right. During the exposure, everyone stays at their assessed position and nobody approaches the vessel. After it, the team confirms safe conditions with the required radiation checks before anyone goes near. Time is saved by preparation and discipline; the exposure itself lasts as long as the image quality needs, because an image that has to be repeated costs more dose than one done properly.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Good preparation also keeps exposure time down.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Before any radiation is produced, the team checks the weld i","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"After it, the team confirms safe conditions with the require","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Time is saved by preparation and discipline; the exposure it","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P5"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Finally, the drawing becomes real only in the workshop. The team checks the actual hall against the plan and carries out the last-minute risk assessment. During the first or a test exposure, they measure at the perimeter and adjust it where the reading asks for it; the shielding and the occupied positions are verified under the work procedure in the same way. And if the access route reopens or conditions change, the work stops and the assessment is made again. That is optimisation in practice: shielding, distance, preparation and supervision working together, with measurement confirming that the arrangements do what the drawing promised.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Finally, the drawing becomes real only in the workshop.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The team checks the actual hall against the plan and carries","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"And if the access route reopens or conditions change, the wo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That is optimisation in practice: shielding, distance, prepa","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P6"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S08-P1","B1.1-S08-P2","B1.1-S08-P3","B1.1-S08-P4","B1.1-S08-P5","B1.1-S08-P6"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"Does the screen protect the whole team?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S09-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Look at the two working positions in Bram's hall. The lead screen stands between the vessel and Daniel's controls. Sofia supervises the other entrance, on the opposite side of the examination area. She is outside the perimeter too, with her personal dosimeter on, and from where she stands she can see the door and the forklift route. What she does not have is the screen: it stands on Daniel's side, and nothing is between her and the vessel.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Same hall; Daniel-screen relationship highlighted, then Sofia on the opposite side. No measured result claimed.","beats":[{"at":"Look at the two working positions in Bram's hall.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The lead screen stands between the vessel and Daniel's contr","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"She is outside the perimeter too, with her personal dosimete","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"What she does not have is the screen: it stands on Daniel's ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S09-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"During the test exposure the team measures at both positions. At Daniel's controls the reading is low. At Sofia's position it meets the applicable dose-rate criterion for that position, and clearly higher than at Daniel's. Sofia says what many of us would say: \"The reading meets the criterion, so I'm fine where I am.\" Bram points to a spot by the door, five metres further back, from which the entrance is still in full view. Luc mentions that a second screen is in the depot and could be here tomorrow.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Same hall; Daniel-screen relationship highlighted, then Sofia on the opposite side. No measured result claimed.","beats":[{"at":"During the test exposure the team measures at both positions","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"At Daniel's controls the reading is low.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Sofia says what many of us would say: \"The reading meets the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Luc mentions that a second screen is in the depot and could ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S09-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"That is the whole of optimisation in one small decision: a position whose reading meets the applicable criterion, two ways to improve it, and a job that has been prepared for today. Keep three things in view: the dose at Sofia's position, the entrance she supervises, and what is reasonable to ask of the team and the client.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Same hall; Daniel-screen relationship highlighted, then Sofia on the opposite side. No measured result claimed.","beats":[{"at":"That is the whole of optimisation in one small decision: a p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Keep three things in view: the dose at Sofia's position, the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-P3"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S09-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Sofia's position","prompt_spoken_once":"What does the team do about Sofia's position?","situation_visible_text":"At Sofia's position the measured dose rate is within the applicable dose-rate criterion but well above Daniel's. Bram offers a spot five metres further back with the entrance still in view. A second screen could arrive tomorrow.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Keep her where she is: the reading at her position is within the applicable criterion, so the arrangement is acceptable.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The reading does tell us something important: the applicable dose-rate criterion is met at this position, and the team was right to measure rather than assume. Respecting the limit is the third principle; optimisation is the second, and it keeps asking whether a reasonable improvement is available. Here one is, at no cost: a position further back that still gives her the entrance. Below the limit, the question is always: is there a better place she can stand?","screen":"The local criterion is met, and a free improvement is still available. Optimisation continues below the limit."},"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Move her to the position by the door, where the entrance is still in view, and measure again during a controlled test exposure before routine work.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Distance is the cheapest protection there is: the farther position offers a practical improvement while the entrance stays supervised. The team verifies the new arrangement and measures there during a controlled test exposure. Routine work continues only if the results confirm adequate protection. Dose reduced, supervision kept, the client's day respected: that is what \"as low as reasonably achievable\" looks like in a hall.","screen":"Further back, entrance still covered, measured again: a reasonable improvement, verified."},"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Postpone the exposures until the second screen arrives tomorrow and put it on Sofia's side.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"A second screen would lower Sofia's dose further, and on a longer job it may well be worth bringing. Optimisation, though, weighs the improvement against what it costs, a day's delay for Bram's plant, a team that stands idle, and against what else is available. Today the team first assesses the available farther position and verifies it by measurement. If that does not provide adequate protection, it must add suitable measures or postpone the job. The screen remains an option to assess, not something cost alone allows us to dismiss.","screen":"A screen helps; a free improvement is available today. Reasonable means weighing the gain against the cost."},"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S09-P1","B1.1-S09-P2","B1.1-S09-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S09-P3","interaction_id":"B1.1-S09-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S10","title":"Dose information: read the right evidence","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We have improved the arrangements for Bram's job. Now look at what the instruments and the dose records can actually tell us, because they answer different questions. Daniel carries three devices. In his hand, the survey meter: it measures the radiation field at a place, right now, at the perimeter, at the control position, next to the vessel after an exposure. On the left of his chest, the electronic personal dosimeter: it follows the dose he himself receives, shows it live and sounds an alarm at a set level. On the right, the passive badge: it records his dose over the monitoring period and is read out afterwards by the dosimetry service, which makes it the official record of what he received. Three devices, three jobs, and all three sit behind the shielding and the perimeter that do the protecting.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"We have improved the arrangements for Bram's job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Daniel carries three devices.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"On the left of his chest, the electronic personal dosimeter:","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Three devices, three jobs, and all three sit behind the shie","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"With those three in mind, keep two quantities apart. A dose rate, in microsieverts per hour, is what the survey meter reads: how fast dose is being delivered at one place at one moment. An accumulated dose, in millisieverts, is what the dosimeters build up: how much a person has received over a period. A rate at the tape and a dose on a badge are different things, so comparing one with a limit meant for the other tells you nothing. To check a personal dose limit, the quantity, the person and the period have to match, with every exposure of that period included, which is why one favourable reading at the perimeter says nothing about Daniel's dose for the year.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"With those three in mind, keep two quantities apart.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"A dose rate, in microsieverts per hour, is what the survey m","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A rate at the tape and a dose on a badge are different thing","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"To check a personal dose limit, the quantity, the person and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Three reference levels guide protection, and each serves a different purpose. The legal dose limit is the boundary that may never be crossed. A dose constraint sits below it: a planning level used in optimisation for a particular job or source, which the Agency can impose. The alarm setting on Daniel's electronic dosimeter is different again: an operational warning threshold, set for this task under our approved arrangements, so that he knows early when the work is not going as planned. Limit, constraint, alarm: boundary, planning level, early warning.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Three reference levels guide protection, and each serves a d","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The legal dose limit is the boundary that may never be cross","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The alarm setting on Daniel's electronic dosimeter is differ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Limit, constraint, alarm: boundary, planning level, early wa","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"So what happens when the alarm sounds in Bram's hall? Daniel acts under the procedure: the exposure is stopped, he moves away from the source, and he reports what happened before anything resumes. The alarm is a signal to act; its cause and the recorded dose still need to be checked. An alarm does not, by itself, establish how the dose compares with a limit. And when the alarm stays silent, the dosimeter has recorded what he received; the proof that the limits were respected comes from the records over the period, read against the right quantity and the right person. The instruments tell us where we are; the planning and the records tell us whether we did well.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"So what happens when the alarm sounds in Bram's hall?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The alarm is a signal to act; its cause and the recorded dos","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"An alarm does not, by itself, establish how the dose compare","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The instruments tell us where we are; the planning and the r","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S10-P1","B1.1-S10-P2","B1.1-S10-P3","B1.1-S10-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S11","title":"Can one reading answer for the week?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S11-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"For this dose-planning example, look ahead to the end of the Havenmeer job. Back at the depot, Daniel reads his electronic dosimeter: a small dose for the day, well within what the plan expected. The survey meter has done its work at the perimeter and at the control position. His passive badge goes back in the rack; the dosimetry service will read it out at the end of the monitoring period, as it does every time.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S11 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"For this dose-planning example, look ahead to the end of the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Back at the depot, Daniel reads his electronic dosimeter: a ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The survey meter has done its work at the perimeter and at t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"His passive badge goes back in the rack; the dosimetry servi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S11-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S11-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Luc is planning the coming days. \"Daniel's reading is low,\" he says, \"so I'll put him on the gamma job tomorrow and the two bunker days after that. No need to look anything up.\" Sofia, listening, isn't so sure: the week's jobs add up, and Daniel had a heavy job last week too. Think about what Luc is holding in his hand, what that number covers, and what the limit is written for.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S11 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Luc is planning the coming days.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"\"Daniel's reading is low,\" he says, \"so I'll put him on the ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"No need to look anything up.\" Sofia, listening, isn't so sur","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Think about what Luc is holding in his hand, what that numbe","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S11-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S11-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Planning Daniel's week","prompt_spoken_once":"What does Luc need before he schedules Daniel's week?","situation_visible_text":"Daniel's electronic dosimeter shows a small dose for today's job. Luc wants to schedule him for a gamma job tomorrow and two bunker days after that, without checking anything. His badge is read out at the end of the period.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Nothing more: today's electronic reading is low, so the limit leaves plenty of room for the week.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Today's reading is real and useful: it tells us this job went as planned. What it covers is one day. The limit is written for a person over a period, and every job in that period counts towards the same total, last week's heavy job included. So the number in Luc's hand is one entry in a running record, and the planning question is answered by that record, with the last entry as one part of it.","screen":"One day's reading is one entry. The limit applies to the period, with every job included."},"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"The readout of Daniel's passive badge for today's job, before anything else is scheduled.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The badge is the official record, and it will confirm the period's dose when the service reads it out. That is exactly why it is read per monitoring period and not per job: it is the check behind the planning. Between readouts, our service keeps Daniel's running dose from the electronic dosimeters and the previous readouts, and that is what Luc looks at before he fills a week.","screen":"The badge confirms the period afterwards. Planning uses the running record kept by the service."},"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Daniel's running dose for the period so far, with the expected doses of the three planned jobs, set against his constraint and the limit.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Three things, matching the way the limit is written: the right person, the right quantity, the right period. The service keeps Daniel's running dose: today's reading, last week's job, the earlier official results and the subsequent operational readings, without counting any exposure twice. Luc adds what the gamma job and the bunker days are expected to give, and reads the total against the planning level set for Daniel and the limit behind it. If the plan meets the applicable requirements, it can be scheduled. Otherwise the service revises the protective arrangements and work allocation. Moving a job to a later day does not reset a person's dose for the period. That is how one low reading becomes a planning decision instead of a guess.","screen":"Running dose for the period plus the expected doses of the planned jobs, against constraint and limit."},"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S11-P1","B1.1-S11-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S11-P2","interaction_id":"B1.1-S11-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S12","title":"The regulation, our licence and our procedures","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now return to the preparation of Bram's job. Planning has accepted the request, and the team is preparing the agreed work. On the desk lie three kinds of document, and Daniel reaches for each of them for a different reason. The first is the regulation: it tells us what has to be done, for everyone who does this work. Article sixteen of the industrial radiography decree, for instance, requires that the safety measures identified in the risk analyses are in place and that the team performs a last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure. That is the requirement, written once, for every job.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Now return to the preparation of Bram's job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"On the desk lie three kinds of document, and Daniel reaches ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The first is the regulation: it tells us what has to be done","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That is the requirement, written once, for every job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The second is our company's licence. It is the Agency's authorisation for our company: it names the installations and equipment we may use, the sources we may hold, the practices we may carry out, industrial radiography in our bunker and on clients' sites, and the conditions attached to all of that. When Daniel wants to know whether we may bring a particular X-ray set to Havenmeer, the licence is the document that answers. Its scope and its conditions are what our company works within, and every job is prepared inside that frame.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The second is our company's licence.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It is the Agency's authorisation for our company: it names t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"When Daniel wants to know whether we may bring a particular ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Its scope and its conditions are what our company works with","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The third is the approved work procedure, and with it the worksite record. The procedure describes how our team performs the work and the checks: in which order, with which instruments, against which criteria. Its radiation-protection content has been examined and approved by the recognised expert, you saw in the earlier scenes how that approval comes about, so when Daniel follows it, the expert's judgement is at the vessel with him. The record is the other half: it shows what was actually checked at Havenmeer, by whom, when, and with what result. The procedure is the method; the record is the evidence that the method was applied today, in this hall, with these results.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The third is the approved work procedure, and with it the wo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The procedure describes how our team performs the work and t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The record is the other half: it shows what was actually che","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The procedure is the method; the record is the evidence that","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Three documents, three questions. What is required? The regulation. What may our company do, and under which conditions? The licence. How do we do it, and what did we actually check? The procedure and its record. Open the three parts of Bram's job file and read, in each one, the line that answers its question.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Three documents, three questions.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The regulation.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"How do we do it, and what did we actually check?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Open the three parts of Bram's job file and read, in each on","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P4"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S12-X01","type":"guided_exploration","title_visible":"What does each part of the file establish?","prompt_spoken_once":"Open the three parts of the job file and read the line each one is there for.","items":[{"id":"regulation","label":"The regulation: what is required?","page":"Extract of the industrial radiography decree, article sixteen, with the two lines in focus: the identified safety measures are present; a last-minute risk assessment is performed before the first exposure.","spoken":"This is the requirement for Bram's job and for every job like it: the safety measures from the risk analyses are in place, and the team carries out its last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure. It is the same for every hall and every team. Which measures those are for Havenmeer, and whether they were checked today, you find in the next two parts.","screen":"Required: assessed safety measures present; last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure.","field_in_focus":"The regulation: what is required?","clip":"B1.1-S12-X01-regulation"},{"id":"licence","label":"Our licence: what may we do, under which conditions?","page":"Teaching excerpt of the company licence, with the fields in focus: authorised practices (radiography in the company bunker and on clients' sites); equipment scope; conditions.","spoken":"This is the Agency's authorisation for our company. It tells Daniel that radiography on a client's site is within our practices, that the X-ray set he plans to bring is within our equipment scope, and which conditions apply. The licence sets the frame for the job; the justification, the risk analyses and today's checks fill that frame in for Havenmeer.","screen":"Licence: authorised practices, equipment scope, conditions.","field_in_focus":"Our licence: what may we do, under which conditions?","clip":"B1.1-S12-X01-licence"},{"id":"procedure","label":"Procedure and record: how, and what was checked?","page":"The worksite set-up procedure with its approval line (recognised expert) in focus; below it, today's worksite record with one completed line: perimeter measured at the first exposure · result · time · Daniel.","spoken":"The procedure tells the team how: mark out the perimeter, measure at the line during the first exposure, enlarge it if the reading asks for it, approved by the recognised expert. The record shows that it happened at Havenmeer: the measurement, the result, the time, and Daniel's name. Together they answer \"how do we work\" and \"what did we do today\", and the record is what the expert and the Agency will read later.","screen":"Procedure: how to check. Record: who checked what, when, with which result.","field_in_focus":"Procedure and record: how, and what was checked?","clip":"B1.1-S12-X01-procedure"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-X01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S12-P1","B1.1-S12-P2","B1.1-S12-P3","B1.1-S12-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S12-P4","interaction_id":"B1.1-S12-X01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S13","title":"The hall is no longer as planned","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Daniel and Sofia arrive at Havenmeer Process Works for the job that was planned last week. Bram meets them at the door of the hall. Everything was prepared on paper: the workpiece, the technique, the protection perimeter, the place for the shielding and the positions of the two radiographers. Daniel walks in and sees two things that were different on paper. Pallets are now stored exactly where the perimeter and the shielding were planned. And in the adjoining hall, behind the wall, a maintenance team is at work. In the plan, that hall was empty.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Daniel and Sofia arrive at Havenmeer Process Works for the j","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Everything was prepared on paper: the workpiece, the techniq","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Pallets are now stored exactly where the perimeter and the s","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"In the plan, that hall was empty.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"These two changes matter because the plan was calculated on the hall as it was described. The distance to the perimeter, the place of the shielding, the positions of Daniel and Sofia and the dose rate at the wall of the adjoining hall all follow from that description. Pallets in the way mean the perimeter can no longer run where it was calculated, and the shielding can no longer stand where it was meant to stand. People in the adjoining hall mean that the wall is now a boundary with someone on the other side. The assessment must include adjoining areas, even when people cannot be seen from the vessel. Article nineteen sets a maximum of ten microsieverts per hour for permanent workstations and adjoining buildings; an apparently empty adjoining area must not simply be ignored. One change moves the perimeter. The other changes what the perimeter has to protect.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"These two changes matter because the plan was calculated on ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Pallets in the way mean the perimeter can no longer run wher","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Article nineteen sets a maximum of ten microsieverts per hou","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The other changes what the perimeter has to protect.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The X-ray set stays switched off and the first exposure waits. Daniel reports to Luc and to our service, and tells Bram what he has found. Then each of them decides their own part. Bram decides what happens in his hall: whether the pallets are moved, and whether the maintenance team stays, pauses or leaves. Our company decides whether the plan still covers the new situation. That means a new look at the perimeter, at the shielding and at the dose rate on every side, including the side it cannot see. If the pallets are gone and the neighbouring work is paused, our team still checks that the agreed conditions really are present before proceeding under the procedure. If the pallets stay or the team keeps working, the plan is adapted, checked and confirmed first. In both cases the start signal comes from the company's own check, after Bram has done his part.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The X-ray set stays switched off and the first exposure wait","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram decides what happens in his hall: whether the pallets a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"That means a new look at the perimeter, at the shielding and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"In both cases the start signal comes from the company's own ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Changed conditions are normal on a site. Halls get used, pallets arrive, other teams are planned in. The skill is to see the change, stop, report it and reassess, instead of fitting the work around it. And the division is clear: the person who owns the hall decides about the hall, and the company that brings the radiation decides about the radiation. Bram can clear the space and move his people. Whether it is safe to expose is a decision our company takes, and it takes that decision with the plan in hand.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Changed conditions are normal on a site.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The skill is to see the change, stop, report it and reassess","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"And the division is clear: the person who owns the hall deci","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Whether it is safe to expose is a decision our company takes","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P4"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S13-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Who decides what?","prompt_spoken_once":"Daniel has found two changes. Who decides what, before the first exposure can start?","situation_visible_text":"Daniel and Sofia arrive at Havenmeer Process Works for the planned on-site job. Pallets are now stored where the protection perimeter and the shielding were planned. A maintenance team is working in the adjoining hall, which the plan assumed to be empty. No exposure has started yet.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Bram clears the pallets and confirms that the maintenance team will take a break during the exposures. With both settled, Daniel starts as planned, because the hall is now as it was described.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have Bram's part right: the pallets and the maintenance team are his to arrange. The piece that is missing is the company's own check. The plan was calculated on an empty adjoining hall and on a perimeter at a certain distance. A break during the exposures is an arrangement, and arrangements are verified and written into the plan before they protect anyone. The hall is only as described when the company has confirmed that itself.","screen":"Bram arranges the hall. The company confirms the plan before the start."},"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Bram clears the pallets and decides whether the maintenance team stays or leaves. Daniel takes his word on the adjoining hall and only re-measures the perimeter on his own side of the wall.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that Bram decides about the pallets and about his own people. Where this goes wrong is the wall. The perimeter belongs to the radiography company on every side, also on the side it cannot see. A boundary that is measured on one side and taken on trust on the other is half a boundary. The company checks the dose rate where people can be, and the adjoining hall is now exactly such a place.","screen":"The perimeter is the company's on every side, including behind the wall."},"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Bram decides what happens to the pallets and the maintenance team, because the hall is his. The company decides whether the new situation is still covered by the plan and checks the setup before exposure and verifies the perimeter during the first or a test exposure.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. Two owners, two decisions. Bram owns the hall, so the pallets and the maintenance team are his to move, pause or keep. The company owns the radiation, so whether the plan still holds, where the perimeter now runs and what the dose rate is on every side are its decisions, with the setup checked beforehand and dose rates measured during the first or a test exposure. Daniel reports to Luc, to our service and to Bram, and the job starts when both parts are done.","screen":"Bram: the hall. The company: the plan, the perimeter and the start."},"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S13-P1","B1.1-S13-P2","B1.1-S13-P3","B1.1-S13-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S13-P4","interaction_id":"B1.1-S13-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S14","title":"From hold to a verified arrangement","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We stay at Havenmeer, because the hold is only the beginning. The first thing Daniel does is report in facts. The space where the shielding and the perimeter were planned is taken by stored pallets. People are at work in the adjoining hall. No exposure has been made. He reports it this way to Luc and to our service, and he writes it down the same way in the worksite file. Facts first, because everyone who now has to decide, Luc, the physical control service and Bram, works from this description and nothing else. A report of what has been seen, what is known and what still has to be established is the ground every next step stands on.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"We stay at Havenmeer, because the hold is only the beginning","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The space where the shielding and the perimeter were planned","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"He reports it this way to Luc and to our service, and he wri","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"A report of what has been seen, what is known and what still","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram does his part: he has the pallets moved and he coordinates with the maintenance team about when they work and where. Meanwhile the company looks at the arrangement as a whole, and that is more than the two things Daniel noticed. Five elements belong together in a site arrangement: the space, the direction of the beam, the shielding, the areas where people can be, and who supervises the perimeter during the exposures. Change one and the others shift with it. A pallet that stays means the shielding moves, and shielding that moves means the beam direction and the perimeter distance are looked at again. The outcome can be that the stored material is moved, that the neighbouring work is rescheduled, or that a different arrangement is assessed and chosen. The outcome can also be that the job waits for another day, because safe conditions are a result that is reached, and sometimes the way to reach them is to come back.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Bram does his part: he has the pallets moved and he coordina","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Five elements belong together in a site arrangement: the spa","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A pallet that stays means the shielding moves, and shielding","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The outcome can also be that the job waits for another day, ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"When the arrangement is decided, the team walks it before anyone exposes. The shielding stands where it is drawn. The perimeter is marked where it is calculated. The agreed arrangements for the adjoining hall are confirmed, and the applicable boundary criterion is included in the checks. The worksite information is updated so the file describes the hall as it is today. Then Daniel and Sofia do their last-minute risk assessment at the spot: a short, deliberate look at the real situation, in the minutes before the first exposure, by the people who will do the work.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"When the arrangement is decided, the team walks it before an","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The perimeter is marked where it is calculated.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The agreed arrangements for the adjoining hall are confirmed","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Then Daniel and Sofia do their last-minute risk assessment a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The first exposure is a test. During it the team measures the dose rate at the perimeter and at the wall of the adjoining hall, and compares the readings with the limits in the plan. Where a reading is higher than planned, the arrangement is adjusted and measured again. The readings that go into the record are the ones from the meter, written at the time, with the place and the moment. That is what makes the arrangement verified: a plan that was calculated, a set-up that was checked, and measurements that confirm it. The permission to continue follows from those readings, and that is where this example ends.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The first exposure is a test.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Where a reading is higher than planned, the arrangement is a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The readings that go into the record are the ones from the m","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The permission to continue follows from those readings, and ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S14-P1","B1.1-S14-P2","B1.1-S14-P3","B1.1-S14-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S15","title":"Bram's assignment: bring the reasoning together","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram's request is where this lesson started, so let us walk his request back from the beginning, this time in one line of reasoning. He asked for radiography on two welds. Before any exposure was made, the company asked three questions, in this order. Is radiography needed for these welds, and on what basis: a standard from a recognised standardisation organisation, or a risk analysis of what an undetected defect would mean? Where will the exposure take place, and does this piece belong in the bunker, or is there a supported reason for his hall? And with what equipment, with an X-ray generator preferred where that is feasible without extra risk? Three questions, three justified answers, and only then a job.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 1.","beats":[{"at":"Bram's request is where this lesson started, so let us walk ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Before any exposure was made, the company asked three questi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Where will the exposure take place, and does this piece belo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Three questions, three justified answers, and only then a jo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"With the job justified, the company organised protection. It drew the perimeter around the work, put distance and shielding between the radiation and the people, and placed two radiographers where they can supervise the perimeter and remain in visual or audible contact. It gave each of them a survey meter for the dose rate at a place and dosimeters for the dose they themselves receive, and it read those numbers against the planning level set for them and the limit behind it. It planned Daniel's week on his running dose for the period, with every job counted. And it wrote all of that down in documents that each answer a different question: what is required, what the company may do, how it is done, and what was done.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 2.","beats":[{"at":"With the job justified, the company organised protection.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It drew the perimeter around the work, put distance and shie","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It planned Daniel's week on his running dose for the period,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And it wrote all of that down in documents that each answer ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Then the hall was different from the plan, and the reasoning showed its value. The team held. Daniel reported facts. Bram arranged his hall, the company reassessed its plan, and the start was made to depend on measurements at the first exposure. Every step you have seen in this lesson belongs to one of three things: justifying the work, protecting the people, and checking that the real situation matches the plan.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"Then the hall was different from the plan, and the reasoning","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The team held.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Bram arranged his hall, the company reassessed its plan, and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Every step you have seen in this lesson belongs to one of th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now Bram calls again. A week later, he has another weld in the same hall. He says: you have the plan from last time, the pallets are gone, the hall is quiet, can you come tomorrow and do the same? It sounds simple, and that is exactly why it is a good test of what you have learned.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"Now Bram calls again.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"A week later, he has another weld in the same hall.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"He says: you have the plan from last time, the pallets are g","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"It sounds simple, and that is exactly why it is a good test ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P4"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"That closes the first lesson, and here is what you now carry with you. You know what a radiography company is and why it exists: it finds defects that eyes cannot see, with radiation that needs rules. You know who is who around that radiation: the Agency that licenses and supervises, the recognised organisation and its expert who examine and approve, the physical control service that watches from inside, the head of that service who makes sure every justification was made by someone competent, the company that refuses a job it cannot accept, and the radiographers who do the work and are trained as agents. You know the three questions that come before every job, technique, location and equipment, and that each has to be justified and written down. You know how the people are protected: with a perimeter, distance, shielding, two radiographers, a survey meter for the dose rate at a place, dosimeters for the dose a person receives, and a planning level below the limit. You know which document answers which question. And you know what to do when the real situation differs from the plan: hold, report facts, let each party decide its own part, and verify with measurements before the start.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"That closes the first lesson, and here is what you now carry","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"You know who is who around that radiation: the Agency that l","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"You know how the people are protected: with a perimeter, dis","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And you know what to do when the real situation differs from","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P5"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Keep three questions with you for every lesson that follows. What is known? What still has to be checked? And who has to act? In B one point two we stay with the same people and make their responsibilities concrete: what the radiation protection agent checks on the day, what the recognised expert approves and how often, and who receives the report when something is found.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"Keep three questions with you for every lesson that follows.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"What is known?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"And who has to act?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"In B one point two we stay with the same people and make the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P6"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S15-R01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Bram's second request","prompt_spoken_once":"What does Bram's second request start in the company?","situation_visible_text":"A week after the first job, Bram asks for radiography on another weld in the same hall. He offers last week's plan, says the pallets are gone and the hall is quiet, and asks whether the team can come tomorrow and do the same.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The same three questions as the first time, for this weld: whether radiography is justified, where it belongs, and with what equipment. Then a plan for the hall as it is on the day, verified at the first exposure.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. A second weld is a second request, and a request starts the reasoning, not the exposure. Justification is about this weld: the standard or the risk analysis that applies to it, and the question whether this piece can go to the bunker. Last week's plan is a useful starting point, and it becomes this week's plan when the hall has been checked as it is tomorrow and the first exposure has been measured. Bram's good news about the pallets is welcome. The company checks it itself.","screen":"A new weld starts the three questions again. Last week's plan is a starting point; tomorrow's hall and the first exposure decide."},"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Last week's plan, because the justification was done for this hall and these workpieces. The team arrives, confirms that the pallets are gone and the hall is quiet, and starts with the same perimeter and measurements.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have remembered that the plan was built with care, and much of it will carry over. The part to look at again is the justification, because we must check whether the existing written justification for the type of assignment covers this new weld and these conditions. The standard or risk analysis, the location and the equipment must remain applicable. And a perimeter is confirmed by measuring at the first exposure, at every job, also in a hall the team knows.","screen":"Check that the written justification covers this assignment type and its conditions; verify the perimeter during the first or a test exposure."},"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"A visit by the recognised expert, because a second job in the same hall makes it a regular site and the expert approves the arrangement. The team waits for that approval and then uses last week's plan.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that the recognised expert has a role, and you will see in the next lesson what the expert approves and when. The decision to accept Bram's request, to justify this weld and to prepare the arrangement lies with the company itself: the head of the physical control service makes sure the justification was made by someone competent, and the team plans and verifies the hall. The expert checks that this system works. Tomorrow's job starts with the company's own three questions.","screen":"The client justifies technique and location; our company checks acceptance, justifies equipment and plans the work. The expert performs the reserved expert tasks."},"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S15-P1","B1.1-S15-P2","B1.1-S15-P3","B1.1-S15-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S15-P4","interaction_id":"B1.1-S15-R01","post_interaction_cues":[{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P5","condition":"after activity completion"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P6","condition":"after activity completion"}]}}]}]};
